;; og:preserve-this (method 70 wvehicle) and *debug-engine-sound-work*
;; (used only inside it) are both omitted rather than landed. This is the
;; dual-purpose sp+96 block the wvehicle-small-tier rung held: the method
;; never converged after thirty-five op patches (reverted), and its own
;; debug-engine-sounds branch separately fails static-ref on
;; *debug-engine-sound-work* (L136, an unparseable <static-data L136>
;; placeholder, the same decompiler gap class as weapon-suppression-
;; table). A skip_compile_functions entry marks the held method so the
;; decomp-vs-REF diff still gates the rest of this object (methods 223,
;; 144, 169, 170 and the five update-engine-mix-state/loop-state types
;; and function above). Re-derive from the framework's own dump (offline-
;; test -f wvehicle-sounds -d) once the sp+96 block and the L136 static
;; both have a real fix.